## Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 §4(b))

What is carried over from deepsec is its ARCHITECTURE, not its source:

- The two-stage pipeline — a free deterministic regex pass that emits
  "candidates", followed by an AI pass that adjudicates each candidate
  into a "finding". This is the core idea and it is deepsec's.
- The matcher record shape (`slug` / `description` / `noiseTier` /
  `filePatterns` / `examples` + a list of `{ regex, label }` pairs).
- The convention of a hand-curated, per-project `INFO.md` context
  document injected into every adjudication prompt.
- The vulnerability-category vocabulary (the `vulnSlug` namespace:
  `auth-bypass`, `ssrf`, `secret-in-log`, and siblings).

What differs:

- All regular expressions are newly authored. No pattern source was
  copied from the deepsec bundle.
- Adjudication runs inside an agentOS VM, driven by the "pi" ACP
  adapter, on a model credential the caller supplies through their own
  environment. There is no Vercel AI Gateway dependency, no Vercel
  project link, and no Vercel Sandbox.
- There is no orchestration layer. A run is a single `runScan` call
  that returns a result and writes one JSON record; deepsec's
  filesystem-checkpoint machinery is not carried over and nothing
  replaces it.
- Adds a multi-tenancy matcher family with no deepsec equivalent
  (`tenancy-unscoped-query`, `actor-key-injection`,
  `trusted-principal-header`, `secret-compare-timing`), plus
  `composeMatchers` so a consumer can merge their own families into the
  default set.
- Drops deepsec's Vercel-specific surface entirely (project linking,
  Sandbox fan-out, gateway credential brokering, the `vercel-setup`
  flow).
- Adds a CLI (`scan` / `init` / `doctor` / `list` / `report` /
  `export`), an on-disk run record, and a measurement suite under
  `bench/` — none of which have a deepsec counterpart.
